<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Andres, with 50 mph winds, is nearing the coast of far southeast Mexico. It is expected to weaken after making landfall and then to continue east-northeast across north Guatemala and Belize. Heavy rain and flooding will be the main problem with this system, especially in western areas. Winds could be a problem along the Pacific coast of far southeast Mexico.</p>
</text>
